adjutant
========

adjutant is a derivative work of PLINK 2.0, cut down to polygenic-score
computation and evaluation.

    PLINK 2.0   https://github.com/chrchang/plink-ng
                (C) 2005-2026 Shaun Purcell, Christopher Chang

**The majority of this code is PLINK 2.0's**, and all of the credit for it
belongs there. adjutant was produced by deleting commands from
`PLINK v2.0.0-a.7.1.a` rather than by writing a scorer from scratch. In
particular the scoring engine, the .pgen/.pvar/.psam readers, the sample and
variant filters, the text and compression layers and the memory allocator are
upstream code, modified little or not at all. If you use adjutant in published
work, cite PLINK 2:

    Chang CC, Chow CC, Tellier LCAM, Vattikuti S, Purcell SM, Lee JJ (2015)
    Second-generation PLINK: rising to the challenge of larger and richer
    datasets. GigaScience 4.

What is not upstream: the PGS evaluation numerics (`adjutant_pgs_eval.*`), the
PGS harmonisation (`adjutant_pgs_match.*`), and the flags that drive them
(`--give-best-pgs`, `--give-corr-matrix`, `--pgs-pheno-pairs`,
`--score-partitions`, `--sscore`, `--pgs-model`, `--pgs-models-list`).


